WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.836
The listing says in stock.

2
00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:05.233
The buyer drives across town; the shelf is empty.

3
00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:10.758
AutoParts Tunisia: a French, mobile-first marketplace for car parts.

4
00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:14.367
No order moves until a human has called the supplier.

5
00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:17.637
Start with the car: make, model, engine.

6
00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:20.607
The catalogue narrows to what fits that engine.

7
00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:25.475
Open a part: the listed price, and the twenty percent deposit, up front.

8
00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:28.255
Ask for it, and an agent phones the shop.

9
00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:33.990
The deposit goes by D17 or bank transfer, proof uploaded from the phone.

10
00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:37.554
An admin checks it; the balance is cash on delivery.

11
00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:40.433
Underneath is one order state machine.

12
00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:43.119
Only the right actor can make each move.

13
00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:47.068
A twenty-four hour clock starts at every deposit request.

14
00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:50.442
Miss it, and a cron fails the order and frees the part.

15
00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:55.861
Storefront, admin queue, supplier dashboard: built by Hamza Benarfa.
